      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Ligand H4L1 (0.05 mmol, ca. 32.1 mg), Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.3 mmol, ca. 135 mg), CH3OH (1 mL), CH3CN (1 mL), and triethylamine (0.10 mL) were added to a Pyrex tube (one end ca. 25 cm long), shaken and sonicated for 15 min, then sealed and heated in an oven at 80 °C. After two days the tube was removed, slowly cooled to room temperature, and yellow lumpy crystals of 1 precipitated.",
